// saatçi's: saat makinesi, İsviçre çapalı eşapman, eşapman çarkı, çapa,
// balans, spiral yay, zemberek, zemberek kutusu, fusee, zincir, pinyon, kurma
// kolu, sütunlu çark, regülatör. One movement cannot have two names for a part.
//
// A case suffix on a number or an identifier rides after an APOSTROPHE and
// OUTSIDE the closing tag — 18,000'den, <code>CLEAR_MARGIN</code>'ın — so the
// checker's number token stops at the mark and the <code> span stays the
// source. Common nouns take their suffixes with no space and no mark, which is
// why the hidden .gloss-variants rows list the suffixed forms the prose uses.
//
// NUMBERS AND <code> ARE NOT TRANSLATED — they are the source constants this
// page exists to quote. Emphasis the English carries as CAPITALS rides the
// wording, never an added tag, and a Turkish capital keeps its dot (İ).
// "modellenmiş" vs "simüle edilmiş" tracks the repo's modelled/simulated
// distinction exactly; HONESTY.tr gates it, and the bare noun «model» is
// deliberately not the honesty word.
